# Music Edit Demo

This project is the data-independent scaffold for the MUSDB18 natural-language
music editing demo. It provides:

- a versioned edit-plan schema;
- controlled Chinese instruction parsing, plus an optional Qwen endpoint;
- project, plan, job, and result persistence;
- a generator adapter interface with fake and ACE-Step HTTP backends;
- target-stem-only compositing with equal-power crossfades;
- a CLI and FastAPI service;
- synthetic-audio tests that do not require MUSDB18.

The `fake` backend performs deterministic DSP transformations. It exists only
to validate orchestration and must not be used to assess model quality. Every
result records its backend name.

## Local setup

```powershell
py -m venv .venv
.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pip install -e ".[api]"
```

Run the data-independent smoke demo:

```powershell
$env:PYTHONPATH = "src"
python -m music_edit_demo synthetic --duration 12
python -m music_edit_demo plan --project-id synthetic-demo --start 3 --end 7 --instruction "把鼓点加密，贝斯更有力量，其他轨保持不变"
python -m music_edit_demo run --plan-id <PLAN_ID>
```

Start the API:

```powershell
$env:PYTHONPATH = "src"
python -m music_edit_demo serve --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8000
```

API documentation is available at `http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs`.

## Runtime configuration

| Variable | Default | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `MUSIC_EDIT_RUNTIME_DIR` | `./runtime` | Projects, plans, jobs, and results |
| `MUSIC_EDIT_PARSER` | `controlled` | `controlled` or `qwen` |
| `MUSIC_EDIT_GENERATOR` | `fake` | `fake` or `ace_step_http` |
| `QWEN_BASE_URL` | empty | OpenAI-compatible base URL |
| `QWEN_API_KEY` | empty | Optional API key |
| `QWEN_MODEL` | `Qwen3-4B-Instruct` | Parser model name |
| `ACE_STEP_BASE_URL` | empty | ACE-Step adapter service URL |

## Current input boundary

The scaffold registers four PCM WAV stems (`vocals`, `drums`, `bass`, and
`other`). The MUSDB18 `.stem.mp4` importer and real model service are connected
after the full dataset and its decoding dependencies are available.

